                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I wanted to like the game but it just doesn't have enough content, there's only 2 enemies in the first stage with a another being adding in the 2nd stage so 3 enemies in the first two area's and you'll be doing a lot of fighting those 3 enemies especially if you die because the area's are randomized so you'll need to find the 2nd area all over again. The first stage only has 2 areas within so it wasn't that bad or hard, but then I got two the 3rd area and it had one of the enemies from the first stage with 2 new enemies so it looks like every new stage only gets 2 new enemies to fight. It's just not engaging enough to constantly be refighting the same enemies over and over. Some of the enemies moves also feel unfair they come out immediately so if your to close to where it starts there no time to move out of the way even if you react fast enough. The game also seems unbalanced enemies I feel have way to much health, you don't deal enough damage even just for the first stage, your healing ability really just makes it take even longer because if you are good you can just dodge and heal whenever you take damage making the fights longer. The concept is good the execution is not.",
